    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 51 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft (possible) duplicate signal on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing computed-field pattern (like `namesakeCount`/`bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n**Behavior**: When a new owner is not a hard duplicate (the pipeline only reaches the new step once `CheckIdentityUnique` passes \u2192 no 409) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id. Otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\n**Changes**:\n- `.../rest/function/owner/AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 new OfficeFloor step; scans persisted owners within the write transaction and sets the two fields on the entity.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired `assignPossibleDuplicate` between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns + accessors.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 ignored the two computed fields in `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, matching the sibling fields; `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` maps them by name.\n- `acceptance/Cp36Tests.java` \u2014 new tests: flagged case (same lastName+postcode, different phone \u2192 `true` + matching id), unique owner (`false`), and same-lastName/different-postcode (`false`).\n\nNote: the two fields are persisted like their siblings, so they're returned both on the create response and on later `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
